<div class="section section--alt">
  <div class="section-narrow">
    <h2 class="reveal">What to Expect: Qigong with Seb</h2>
    <ul class="features reveal">
      <li>Genuine, unadulterated Qigong - as it should be</li>
      <li>A welcoming atmosphere for all abilities</li>
      <li>Sessions lasting 60 to 75 minutes</li>
      <li>Five-Element Qigong forms</li>
      <li>Extraordinary-Meridian Qigong forms</li>
      <li>Shen (higher awareness) Qigong forms and esoteric practices</li>
      <li>Bagua Chun Gen (a versatile energy-gate-opening form)</li>
      <li>Medical Qigong elements for practitioners of Tui Na, An Mo, Shiatsu, Nuad Thai, etc.</li>
      <li>Self-care and healing Qigong for those with chronic ailments or disabilities</li>
      <li>Zhan Zhuang - challenging yet deeply rewarding standing postures that develop endurance, rooted stability and explosive vitality</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="intro-link-box reveal">
      <p>New to Qigong?</p>
      <a href="/intro/">Read: Introduction to Authentic Practice</a>
    </div>

    <h2 class="reveal">What to Expect: Yoga & Sound Healing with Jenny / Amy</h2>
    <ul class="features reveal">
      <li>Therapeutic Yoga - focused on healing, recovery and supporting specific physical and emotional needs</li>
      <li>Restorative Yoga - a core part of Jenny's curriculum, using supported postures to encourage deep rest and nervous system regulation</li>
      <li>Vinyasa Yoga - a dynamic, flowing practice linking breath and movement</li>
      <li>Hatha Yoga - a grounded practice building strength, flexibility and awareness</li>
      <li>Yin Yoga - long-held postures working deep into connective tissue and meridian lines</li>
      <li>Sound Healing with Tibetan singing bowls and crystal bowls integrated into yoga sessions</li>
      <li>Breathwork and guided meditative elements</li>
      <li>A calm, supportive space for all levels</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
